==Trivia==
*The word "''Prince''" and by extention "''Princess''" comes from the Latin word "''prīnceps''", meaning first head.
**The Princess is 1 of 20 [[cards]] associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Royal Giant]], [[Royal Delivery]], [[Tower Princess]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Prince]], [[Raging Prince]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Spirit Empress]], [[Super Knight]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Royal Chef]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
*Although the Princess' leggings are team-colored in official Clash Royale promotional videos and renders, they are colored to appear bare on in-game sprites.
*The Princess is 1 of 10 cards associated with archery, with the others being [[Archers]], [[Arrows]], Tower Princess, [[X-Bow]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Super Archers]], Archer Queen, and the Little Prince.
*The Princess was one of the first {{Rarity|Legendary}} [[cards]] to be added to the game, alongside the [[Ice Wizard]].
*The Princess' stats are the highest or lowest among all troops. More specifically:
**The Princess has the longest range of all troops, with a range of 9 tiles.
***The Princess is the only troop that has a higher range than [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]].
***It is theoretically possible to win a [[Basics of Battle|battle]] with just a Princess, due to her range being able to outrange Crown Towers, and is 1 of 2 troops that can do a 3-Crown victory by herself at even Levels, along with the [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Super Mini P.E.K.K.A]].
**The Princess is tied with [[Hog Rider]], Royal Hogs, [[Mother Witch|Cursed Hog]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Terry]] for the longest sight range of all troops, with a sight range of 9.5 tiles.
*The [[Ranked|Grand Champion League]] badge resembles a Princess' crown.
*The Princess has 3 arrows nocked in the card picture, while she only nocks 1 arrow in-game. However, she shoots 5 arrows in-game.
*When spawning, she may say "''Let's go!''"  or "''Yay!''". When attacking, she may say "''Gotcha!''", "''Pew!''", or "''Bullseye!''".  
**The Princess is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Wizard]], Hog Rider, [[P.E.K.K.A.]], Dark Prince, [[Bowler]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Electro Wizard]], Ice Wizard, [[Magic Archer]], [[Lumberjack]], Mother Witch, [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], Super Mini P.E.K.K.A., Santa Hog Rider, [[Super Magic Archer]], Golden Knight, [[Boss Bandit]], Archer Queen, Little Prince, and the Terry.
*The Princess, along with the Archers, [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, [[Musketeer]], Wizard, [[Witch]], and Prince, is featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama].
*The Princess is the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
**The [https://clashroyale.fandom.com/wiki/Emotes?file=Muscle_Princess.png Princess Muscle Emote] is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosie_the_Riveter Rosie the Riveter].
*A [[Clone|cloned]] Princess does not fall from the sky when deployed.
*The Princess was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Princess was featured in the winning deck of the [https://youtu.be/LWQjS0e6iiE Super Magical Cup Tournament], by a player called CMcHugh.
**The Princess was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/psZXKWHkKkE?si=PbjvbZt8stghz6eJ King's Cup II Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
*Before the Princess' [[Cards|card]] release, the Princess' damage was decreased by 6%.

